WEBVTT

00:01.790 --> 00:04.000
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

00:04.920 --> 00:09.460
Spanning more than 400 years
since the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

00:09.880 --> 00:12.000
The goddess enshrined here...

00:15.330 --> 00:17.000
N-nice, very nice!

00:18.210 --> 00:21.540
The intensity of urban warfare
is definitely coming through!

00:22.710 --> 00:29.420
<b>Reflector</b>

00:23.130 --> 00:27.630
...was an absolute social recluse of an elf,
summoned from another world.

00:30.080 --> 00:35.790
Dioramas are so much fun!
It looks like the real thing through a lens!

00:36.210 --> 00:38.000
Is this what they mean by "Gram-worthy?"

00:38.000 --> 00:43.420
Not quite. This is what they mean by "Gram-worthy!"

00:44.000 --> 00:45.380
Isuzu Koimari-chan!

00:45.630 --> 00:49.540
She's got 150,000 followers,
and she's even been on TV recently!

00:49.750 --> 00:52.540
She's an in... influenzar?

00:52.540 --> 00:54.170
"Influencer?"

00:54.170 --> 00:56.710
Yeah, that! A Kanazawa influenzar!

00:56.830 --> 00:59.420
You're bad at using those loan words, huh?

00:59.630 --> 01:02.710
Hm? Koimari in Kanazawa?

01:03.330 --> 01:05.750
No, it couldn't be...

02:44.170 --> 02:48.750
<b>EPISODE 8</b>

02:44.170 --> 02:48.750
<b>HER AND THE</b>

02:44.170 --> 02:48.750
<b>ELF'S SITUATION</b>

02:46.250 --> 02:49.210
<b>PLEASE LET US KNOW</b>

02:46.250 --> 02:49.210
<b>IF YOU NEED ANYTHING</b>

02:49.290 --> 02:50.960
Hup... Hup...

02:52.080 --> 02:54.830
Gonna have to stock up on more amulets soon.

02:55.170 --> 02:56.130
Hello?

02:57.210 --> 03:01.420
Hello! Would you like a shrine seal or an amu...let?

03:07.330 --> 03:09.290
You're the miko-san from the Koganei family, yes?

03:10.000 --> 03:12.000
Might Elda be in the inner shrine?

03:13.460 --> 03:14.250
E-E...

03:15.210 --> 03:18.750
Elda, Elda, Elda! Elda, Elda, Elda! Elda, Elda, Elda!

03:18.750 --> 03:20.830
Elda, Elda, Elda, Elda, Elda!

03:21.040 --> 03:22.290
Elda!

03:22.670 --> 03:24.960
Wh-what is it? What's wrong, Koito?!

03:25.130 --> 03:29.250
Th-th-th-there's some sort of sparkling,
Gram-worthy elf out here!

03:31.040 --> 03:32.040
Haira!

03:34.630 --> 03:37.330
ELDA-CHAN! I'VE MISSED YOU!

03:37.460 --> 03:40.790
Elda-chan, Elda-chan, Elda-chan, Elda-chan!

03:41.540 --> 03:42.880
E-er...

03:43.460 --> 03:44.630
What is it?

03:45.210 --> 03:47.380
Elda looks like she's suffocating...

03:49.710 --> 03:53.710
My apologies. I unfortunately lost my composure earlier.

03:54.290 --> 03:55.710
It's been around 200 years, right?

03:55.830 --> 03:59.920
<b>Uramimi Shrine - Enshrined Deity "Uramimi Hime-no-Mikoto"</b>

03:55.830 --> 03:59.920
<b>Real Name: Hylaria Aira Mirarasta (Age 726)</b>

03:56.290 --> 03:59.710
What a relief that you seem to look healthy, Elda-chan.

03:59.920 --> 04:03.080
Y-yes... You look well, too, Haira.

04:03.170 --> 04:09.330
Koito-chan. As Tsukishima's local deity,
does Elda-chan carry out her daily activities diligently?

04:09.500 --> 04:14.790
She doesn't have a milimeter of diligence,
but she gets along very well with the parishioners.

04:15.380 --> 04:16.380
Have some tea.

04:16.460 --> 04:17.540
My, thank you.

04:17.790 --> 04:21.630
More importantly, let me know
before you come visit, Haira!

04:21.830 --> 04:24.170
We have things we have to do, you know.

04:26.040 --> 04:28.580
Uh... Sh-she made her mad!

04:29.500 --> 04:33.330
Elda-chan... I'm sure I've told you before...

04:34.250 --> 04:35.710
...but you must...

04:36.460 --> 04:38.500
...address me as "Big Sister"!

04:39.830 --> 04:40.920
<b>Big Sister</b>

04:43.790 --> 04:45.790
Call me "Big Sister."

04:45.790 --> 04:48.880
I can hear you! I heard you and I ignored you!

04:49.170 --> 04:52.960
H-hey, is Haira-sama your older sister, Elda?

04:53.080 --> 05:00.130
Sh-she isn't. Haira is the Kanazawa elf,
summoned by Lord Toshiie Maeda.

05:00.460 --> 05:02.540
Since she's 100 years older than us,

05:00.710 --> 05:09.290
<b>Age 621</b>

05:01.170 --> 05:09.290
<b>Age 622</b>

05:01.710 --> 05:09.290
<b>Age 726</b>

05:02.790 --> 05:05.830
she treats me and Yolde like children.

05:06.250 --> 05:09.000
I don't quite understand elves' sense of age...

05:09.380 --> 05:13.880
Koito-chan, it must be a burden
to serve as Elda-chan's miko, isn't it?

05:14.210 --> 05:18.670
I was constantly spoiling her
when she was around 200 years old.

05:18.670 --> 05:21.750
Hey, Haira! W-we're right in front of my miko!

05:22.000 --> 05:27.210
No need to be embarrassed,
it isn't shameful to be so pampered.

05:27.380 --> 05:30.130
Stop, I'm gonna die! I'm gonna die of embarrassment!

05:30.130 --> 05:32.710
Oh come now, elves are immortal.

05:33.750 --> 05:38.500
I wonder if she feels more like a big sister,
or a mother, or something to Elda and other elves.

05:38.500 --> 05:41.080
She sparkles like a princess.

05:41.460 --> 05:43.920
The Maeda clan is well-known
for the Kaga-hyakumangoku hot spring inn,

05:44.040 --> 05:45.630
and it feels like she's a celebrity!

05:46.170 --> 05:49.460
S-so, why did you come to Tokyo?

05:49.750 --> 05:53.670
Starting tomorrow, there will be an exhibition
for products of Kanazawa here.

05:54.170 --> 06:00.330
It's the perfect opportunity to spread the charm of
our home, Kanazawa. I thought I would help out as well.

06:00.330 --> 06:02.580
Huh? As an enshrined deity?!

06:02.790 --> 06:06.920
Yes. Kanazawa is where my beloved parishioners live.

06:07.170 --> 06:10.960
Actually, it hurts my heart that this is all I can do for them.

06:11.380 --> 06:14.290
Wh-what a noble sentiment!

06:15.630 --> 06:18.670
I don't appreciate you looking at her that way.

06:19.460 --> 06:23.420
By the way, are you not with your miko, Haira-sama?

06:23.710 --> 06:31.960
We'll be meeting up tomorrow. She had work to attend to
in Kanazawa, so I came to Tokyo on my own.

06:32.380 --> 06:35.960
My miko is 16 years old, just like you, Koito-chan.

06:36.330 --> 06:38.250
I do hope you two will become friends.

06:38.250 --> 06:41.210
Oh, okay! I can't wait to meet her.

06:42.080 --> 06:46.250
But lately, she won't speak to me much.

06:46.630 --> 06:48.130
She may be in her rebellious stage.

06:48.750 --> 06:52.670
You two get along well. Is there some trick to it?

06:53.170 --> 06:53.880
Huh?

06:55.170 --> 06:59.420
Maybe doing what I'm supposed to do
at the very last moment before my miko gets angry?

06:59.830 --> 07:03.040
It's just that Elda's miko
has no time for a rebellious stage.

07:04.630 --> 07:08.250
Hup, hup, hup...

07:09.460 --> 07:14.670
Oh no, this won't do! I've forgotten
to give you the souvenirs I brought!

07:16.290 --> 07:18.830
It's fresh, so please eat it soon.

07:19.080 --> 07:21.960
Whoa! I'm so glad to get a gift from Kanazawa!

07:22.210 --> 07:26.540
What pretty wrapping paper!
The contents must be super sparkly, too...

07:29.580 --> 07:31.170
It's... grass, huh?

07:32.330 --> 07:33.290
It's grass.

07:35.420 --> 07:37.330
Yes, it is grass!

07:37.790 --> 07:43.040
One of the seven spring herbs, Nazuna,
is awfully delicious when made into tempura.

07:39.420 --> 07:41.250
<b>Nazuna (Shepherd's Purse)</b>

07:43.330 --> 07:45.080
It also goes by Penpen Grass,

07:44.920 --> 07:46.880
<b>Penpen Grass</b>

07:45.420 --> 07:49.670
and it is an extremely lucky food that is said
to cleanse any impurities by rubbing it.

07:50.460 --> 07:56.630
O-oh! Penpe... Nazuna!
So it's delicious, eh, this Penpe... Nazuna!

07:56.790 --> 08:00.330
It is. Well, um...

08:00.330 --> 08:08.960
Actually, my miko gave me money for the gift,
but... it's gone missing for various reasons.

08:09.750 --> 08:13.380
So... I got this Nazuna growing on the side of the road...

08:13.540 --> 08:16.830
What?! If you dropped your money,
we have to go to the police!

08:16.830 --> 08:20.830
N-no, I dropped it at a lottery ticket stand...

08:21.380 --> 08:25.830
I suppose I dropped it, or I lost it all,
or I scratched it away...

08:26.040 --> 08:27.080
I had a feeling...

08:27.080 --> 08:27.880
Huh?

08:28.420 --> 08:31.750
Haira! You still haven't gotten over
your love of gambling?!

08:32.880 --> 08:37.580
A-at Kanazawa Station, there's a lottery shop
called Hyakubangai Chance Center.

08:37.830 --> 08:42.000
I bought a 200 yen ticket
to comfort myself about traveling alone....

08:42.000 --> 08:43.000
<b>Lottery</b>

08:42.420 --> 08:47.080
Surprisingly, I kept losing over and over,
and before I realized it, the souvenir money was...

08:43.000 --> 08:47.750
<b>Scratch</b>

08:43.000 --> 08:47.750
<b>Scratch</b>

08:43.000 --> 08:47.750
<b>Scratch</b>

08:43.000 --> 08:47.750
<b>Scratch</b>

08:43.000 --> 08:47.750
<b>Scratch</b>

08:43.000 --> 08:47.750
<b>Scratch</b>

08:47.750 --> 08:50.290
U-um, then basically...

08:50.290 --> 08:53.250
Haira has had a weakness for gambling for a long time,

08:53.790 --> 08:57.630
and even in the Edo days she was so crazy
about tomikuji, it was a problem!

08:58.250 --> 08:59.380
Tomikuji?

08:59.790 --> 09:02.380
It was a lottery-type thing in the Edo Period...

09:02.380 --> 09:06.130
It was municipal gambling,
done under the approval of the shogunate!

09:06.670 --> 09:11.420
A numbered ticket was put into a box,
and the ticket that was pierced with a pick won the prize.

09:11.710 --> 09:14.670
The first place prize was worth more
than a hundred ryou!

09:14.960 --> 09:18.580
In today's currency, it was around 5 to 10 million yen.

09:18.830 --> 09:20.880
It was incredibly intense.

09:21.250 --> 09:27.330
However, it's popularity gradually declined due to the
momentum of the illegal tomikuji called "kagetomi."

09:27.460 --> 09:30.580
In the end, it was all banned by the shogunate.

09:31.130 --> 09:34.880
And you tried to take part in the kagetomi
when you came to Edo, too, right?

09:35.130 --> 09:37.210
Yolde and I worked like crazy to stop you.

09:37.500 --> 09:40.250
My miko at the time was absolutely furious.

09:40.880 --> 09:45.630
But... it's true. This is my fault.

09:46.830 --> 09:50.880
Misappropriating all the money for souvenirs
and the hotel is such an outlandish thing to do...

09:51.210 --> 09:53.420
So you used up the hotel money?

09:53.880 --> 09:59.000
But it's okay! There will be a major race
at the Tokyo horse racing track soon!

09:59.130 --> 10:02.630
With the dough I've got left,
I can make a hundred times more than what I have!

10:03.290 --> 10:06.630
She just referred to money as "dough"...

10:07.210 --> 10:10.130
You say that then you always end up flat broke.

10:10.500 --> 10:16.670
It's okay, it's fine! The losses I've had up until now
are more like savings, so it's going to be a massive win!

10:16.790 --> 10:20.420
Then that was your true motive for coming to Tokyo?!

10:21.330 --> 10:24.580
And that's why I would love it if you let me stay the night.

10:24.580 --> 10:27.880
Oh, we're back to this huh?
I don't mind hosting you, though.

10:28.460 --> 10:32.290
A-And I thought I was seeing
the elf of all elves for the first time...

10:32.580 --> 10:35.500
I apologize for that, humankind.

10:37.580 --> 10:40.830
Goodness, you haven't changed a bit Haira.

10:41.130 --> 10:44.080
You should've just told the truth from the very beginning.

10:45.710 --> 10:52.040
It's true that I came to help with the exhibition.
And it's also true that I wanted to see the Japan Derby.

10:52.540 --> 10:54.380
However, the absolute truth is...

10:55.880 --> 11:00.330
I wanted to see your face, Elda-chan.

11:03.210 --> 11:04.670
Ugh, jeez!

11:06.290 --> 11:08.250
Oh, Elda, she's so bashful!

11:08.670 --> 11:13.250
Oh, but just go watch the horse races!
No betting on horses!

11:13.250 --> 11:15.500
H-how cruel of you!

11:17.330 --> 11:20.170
Okay, I'll prepare a futon for you in the inner shrine.

11:20.460 --> 11:22.250
Elda's room is too cramped.

11:22.580 --> 11:24.920
Thank you, Koito-chan.

11:29.830 --> 11:33.960
Ah, is that a visitor? He... Eh?!

11:39.920 --> 11:41.250
Isuzu-chan?!

11:42.500 --> 11:46.920
E-Elda! Th-the Isuzu-chan
I showed you earlier! The influenzar!

11:46.920 --> 11:48.500
That's "influencer."

11:48.670 --> 11:52.130
Oh my, Isuzu. Why are you here?

11:52.250 --> 11:52.960
Huh?

11:53.500 --> 11:57.460
I got everything cleared away faster
than expected for my job.

11:57.580 --> 11:59.790
Huh?! Wha-?! What's going on?!

12:00.750 --> 12:06.290
I'll introduce her. This girl is my miko, Isuzu Koimari.

12:06.460 --> 12:09.330
<b>Uramimi Shrine - Miko</b>

12:06.460 --> 12:09.330
<b>Isuzu Koimari (Age: 16)</b>

12:11.170 --> 12:13.500
WHAAAAAAAAAAAAT?!

12:13.500 --> 12:17.330
Oh, Koimari... I knew it.

12:24.040 --> 12:27.130
I'm so glad we didn't miss each other, Isuzu.

12:27.420 --> 12:30.130
How did you know that I was here?

12:30.580 --> 12:33.330
I didn't really consider you being here, Haira.

12:34.080 --> 12:37.830
I was just thinking I'd come say hello
because I was headed somewhere nearby.

12:38.130 --> 12:39.670
I-I see.

12:40.420 --> 12:43.630
Huh... things are kinda feeling a little tense...

12:43.830 --> 12:47.420
Th-that's right, she said her miko
was in her rebellious stage.

12:48.040 --> 12:53.080
But you really surprised me!
I'm always checking out your Insta, Isuzu-chan!

12:53.290 --> 12:56.210
K-Koito is a fan of yours, Isuzu.

12:56.330 --> 12:59.460
C-can you two miko become friends?

13:00.170 --> 13:02.210
I guess. Sure.

13:06.000 --> 13:10.000
My heart has turned to stone. I'll leave the rest to you.

13:10.250 --> 13:13.250
Y-you're way more reserved than I imagined, Isuzu-chan.

13:13.460 --> 13:18.130
I'm sorry. This girl is kind-natured but she can be blunt...

13:18.500 --> 13:21.670
And that's why she has so few friends
and I worry about her.

13:21.670 --> 13:24.710
Be quiet, Haira. Don't treat me like a child.

13:25.380 --> 13:27.830
Oh, that's right. Here, Elda-sama.

13:27.830 --> 13:28.630
Huh?

13:29.630 --> 13:37.040
I-it's... Hokuriku soul food! Beaver arare rice crackers!
I've always wanted to try it just once!

13:31.420 --> 13:37.040
<b>WHITE SHRIMP</b>

13:31.420 --> 13:37.040
<b>BEAVER</b>

13:31.420 --> 13:37.040
<b>BEAVER</b>

13:37.420 --> 13:42.040
I think Haira also brought some souvenirs,
but it seems like they don't sell these here.

13:42.040 --> 13:44.040
Isuzu, you're such a nice girl!

13:44.040 --> 13:45.630
The stone's been lifted, huh?

13:46.580 --> 13:49.290
Goodness, I don't know what I'd do
if I'd gotten more grass, and the-

13:49.290 --> 13:50.630
Elda-chan, shhh!

13:50.830 --> 13:51.420
Huh?

13:51.420 --> 13:54.790
I-it's nothing! Right, Elda-chan?!

13:56.250 --> 13:59.420
Haira-sama, Elda's suffocating again.

14:02.000 --> 14:05.500
But Isuzu, you finished your work
much earlier than anticipated.

14:05.880 --> 14:09.250
It was just taking pictures with the people
of the tourism division and the Kenrokuen Gardens,

14:09.330 --> 14:10.790
and the weather was good.

14:10.790 --> 14:16.880
Oh, that makes sense. I don't fully understand
what the job of an influencer is yet.

14:17.080 --> 14:22.420
That's so awesome, Isuzu-chan!
You're super popular with girls around our age!

14:22.420 --> 14:27.040
Well, I suppose, it might be something
like what we called a "teahouse girl" in the Edo days.

14:27.130 --> 14:29.000
Ah, like at a roadside teahouse?

14:29.210 --> 14:31.710
Teahouse girl? Is that like a waitress?

14:31.960 --> 14:36.500
Yes, at a place like what we'd call a cafe nowadays.

14:37.080 --> 14:40.460
There were girls in the town that were popular like idols.

14:41.000 --> 14:45.960
There was even a ranking called the "Teahouse Girls
Choice List" because they were so popular.

14:46.130 --> 14:47.460
Wow!

14:47.830 --> 14:50.750
At the time, they were depicted
in the latest form of media,

14:50.750 --> 14:53.380
ukiyo-e, and their popularity spread more and more,

14:53.580 --> 14:57.000
and the one who was especially popular
was Kasamori Osen-chan!

14:57.420 --> 14:59.790
She was pretty much an influenzar, huh!

14:59.790 --> 15:05.250
That's "influencer." I was also a big fan
of Osen-chan at the beginning, but...

15:05.540 --> 15:09.000
in the end, I ended up liking
every one of the teahouse girls.

15:09.630 --> 15:14.210
<b>Band Aficionado</b>

15:09.670 --> 15:11.290
You're the type to stan everyone in an entire group.

15:11.630 --> 15:14.210
<b>Box Bet</b>

15:11.710 --> 15:13.830
And the type to do a box bet at races!

15:15.250 --> 15:16.380
Anyways.

15:16.960 --> 15:20.000
Earlier you said you got some grass,
didn't you, Elda-sama?

15:20.000 --> 15:22.880
Gulp! I-is she making a delayed joke?!

15:24.040 --> 15:28.500
Haira, don't tell me...
You didn't use the souvenir money, did you?

15:30.790 --> 15:33.540
Well, but you did promise me, right?

15:34.130 --> 15:36.290
You said you'd quit gambling.

15:36.750 --> 15:41.500
Y-yes... that's true... I did say that.

15:43.790 --> 15:48.460
We both understand.
If Isuzu finds out, there will be bloodshed.

15:44.790 --> 15:50.420
<b>MIKO PUNCH</b>

15:44.790 --> 15:50.420
<b>BLOODSHED</b>

15:44.790 --> 15:50.420
<b>BLOODSHED</b>

15:49.000 --> 15:50.210
And I think...

15:50.790 --> 15:55.880
She made that promise and still spent it all?
This elf, jeez...

15:56.580 --> 15:59.210
We have to change the subject!

15:59.750 --> 16:04.130
I..Isuzu-chan! This is the snack that was introduced
by a basketball player, right?!

16:04.330 --> 16:05.750
Huh? Yeah.

16:05.750 --> 16:09.540
I-I took pictures, too! These are called Gongem!

16:09.540 --> 16:11.380
I don't like robots.

16:11.580 --> 16:15.750
Hold on, Gongem aren't robots, they're M.S.

16:15.750 --> 16:18.080
And super robots, in the first place, are-

16:18.080 --> 16:19.540
Elda, calm down.

16:19.960 --> 16:22.630
Oh my, we've wasted no time becoming friends!

16:22.750 --> 16:25.290
Haira-sama, please be quiet!
Haira, please be quiet!<b></b>

16:25.540 --> 16:31.420
Well, whatever. Haira, we don't want to be
too much of a bother, so let's head to the hotel.

16:31.420 --> 16:34.290
U-um... R-right.

16:34.710 --> 16:36.830
You've already checked in, right?

16:36.830 --> 16:39.420
Um... n-not quite yet, maybe...

16:39.420 --> 16:41.290
You made a reservation, didn't you?

16:41.460 --> 16:45.460
I may have made one... or maybe I cancelled it...

16:45.460 --> 16:48.040
What?! Cancelled?! Why?!

16:48.210 --> 16:49.580
I..Isuzu-chan!

16:49.580 --> 16:54.580
Haira-sama would like to talk to Elda who she hasn't
seen in awhile, so it was decided she'd stay the night.

16:55.000 --> 16:59.420
Th-that's right! I've got 200 years worth
of stories piled up!

16:59.420 --> 17:02.790
A-and you've taken the time
to come all the way from Kanazawa...

17:03.380 --> 17:05.000
Oh, really?

17:05.420 --> 17:09.170
Yeah! So, you stay the night here, too, Isuzu-chan!

17:09.500 --> 17:10.790
Eh? Are you sure?

17:10.790 --> 17:15.750
Of course! I also want to talk with you a lot more,
Isuzu-chan! Sleep in my room!

17:17.540 --> 17:19.500
Then, I accept.

17:23.040 --> 17:27.040
I just bought more meat and veggies today, too!

17:27.210 --> 17:30.380
N-nice timing! You're the best, Koyuzu.

17:34.750 --> 17:37.830
Here you go! It's perfectly charred!

17:37.830 --> 17:39.420
Th-thank you.

17:39.880 --> 17:43.880
Oh dear, you've got some on you.
Let your big sister get that for you.

17:43.880 --> 17:46.750
S-stop it, not in front of the miko!

17:53.250 --> 17:58.290
It feels like a dream that you're staying at my house,
Isuzu-chan! I'm embarassed by my old house, though.

17:58.830 --> 18:00.710
My house is like this, too.

18:01.170 --> 18:04.420
Was it okay to let Haira stay with Elda-sama?

18:05.000 --> 18:06.880
Won't she disturb Elda's sleep?

18:07.290 --> 18:09.500
Elda's a night owl, so it'll be okay!

18:10.670 --> 18:12.670
Say... can I ask you something?

18:12.920 --> 18:13.630
Hm?

18:14.080 --> 18:17.830
Why are things so strained
between you and Haira-sama?

18:20.000 --> 18:24.210
In the past, I've told Haira
that I wanted her to refrain from gambling.

18:24.670 --> 18:30.040
I thought she'd never stop, but she promised me
that she wouldn't do it anymore.

18:30.830 --> 18:34.540
But Haira is playing within the limits of her allowance,

18:35.000 --> 18:39.750
and I felt like a child for being so mean
about what other people liked.

18:40.920 --> 18:46.630
I don't know what kind of expression
I should face Haira with anymore. So that's why.

18:46.830 --> 18:47.540
Oh, I see.

18:48.170 --> 18:52.880
No, she's totally busted right through that limit!
With the souvenir money and the hotel money, too!

18:53.130 --> 18:59.330
I-I gotta make sure I don't eventually let it spill.
If I'm careless it's gonna end with a huge boom!

18:59.500 --> 19:02.880
You and Elda-sama look like
you get along so well, I'm jealous.

19:03.250 --> 19:07.080
That is so not true!
Elda spends her days slacking and being a slob!

19:03.250 --> 19:05.250
<b>Red, maybe...</b>

19:05.790 --> 19:07.790
<b>Nah, maybe blue...</b>

19:07.380 --> 19:08.960
What? Really?

19:08.960 --> 19:10.500
Yeah, she really does!

19:10.630 --> 19:13.750
She secretly buys expensive toys,
and we've even fought about that!

19:13.750 --> 19:18.710
Compared to Elda's slobbishness,
Haira-sama's love of gambling is downright cute!

19:18.540 --> 19:20.540
<b>Ooh,</b>

19:18.540 --> 19:20.540
<b>a butterfly</b>

19:19.000 --> 19:22.880
Just spending all the souvenir
and hotel money is practically nothing!

19:23.290 --> 19:23.750
<b>Snip</b>

19:24.380 --> 19:27.790
"Spending the souvenir and hotel money"?

19:35.500 --> 19:40.960
How dare she give weeds as a souvenir!
And, Haira hasn't stopped gambling, has she?!

19:40.960 --> 19:45.040
I-I am so sorry, Isuzu-chan.
It felt like I was keeping it from you...

19:45.330 --> 19:49.580
No, you and Elda are not at fault here!
The blame falls on...

19:51.750 --> 19:52.710
Well, it's fine.

19:55.080 --> 19:59.960
If Haira is doing what she likes to do,
then I suppose that's a relief.

20:00.670 --> 20:05.500
Isuzu-chan... You're a really kind person,
just like Haira-sama said.

20:06.920 --> 20:13.750
You're really great, Isuzu-chan. As a miko, and a student,
and a influencer, you're doing your best at all of them.

20:14.330 --> 20:22.420
That isn't true. At our shrine the miko takes over
at age 8. I've been with Haira since I was a child.

20:23.000 --> 20:27.380
I admired Haira, and I just wanted
to become an adult as soon as possible.

20:28.170 --> 20:30.540
Th-this sounds familiar...

20:33.040 --> 20:37.080
You want to become a cool adult
so that you can be next to her, right?

20:37.420 --> 20:38.670
Exactly!

20:38.710 --> 20:40.290
You get me, Koito-chan!

20:40.580 --> 20:44.130
Yeah... maybe I'll give you something special.

20:49.500 --> 20:50.420
What's this?

20:50.580 --> 20:53.710
I make these as a hobby. Photo portraits of Haira.

20:54.000 --> 20:57.380
When I get paid, I almost always give
most of my money to the print shop.

20:57.630 --> 20:59.790
Koito-chan, which Haira do you like?

21:00.500 --> 21:01.170
Huh?

21:01.460 --> 21:02.920
It's fine! Choose one!

21:03.040 --> 21:05.790
Ah, err... This one, maybe?

21:05.920 --> 21:09.000
Oh! Because it uses a rare process, huh?

21:09.170 --> 21:13.040
But it's all good! I don't mind
giving it to you, Koito-chan! Here!

21:13.420 --> 21:14.960
Th-thanks...

21:15.830 --> 21:21.880
I see... So the system is if Isuzu-chan is happy,
she'll give you one. I don't want it, though.

21:22.460 --> 21:25.580
Isuzu-chan, you like Haira-sama a lot, don't you?

21:25.580 --> 21:27.500
Huh? Of course I do.

21:31.040 --> 21:33.000
I was scolded so harshly...

21:33.380 --> 21:35.580
I-I'm sorry, Haira-sama...

21:35.580 --> 21:39.580
It's not your fault, Koito-chan.
Haira is to blame for everything.

21:39.580 --> 21:41.710
I-I will reflect on what I've done.

21:42.830 --> 21:45.250
Well then, let's go, Isuzu.

21:45.250 --> 21:46.080
Okay.

21:46.790 --> 21:48.330
Give Koyuzu-chan our regards.

21:48.710 --> 21:50.830
You two are going to hang out at the exhibition, huh?

21:51.040 --> 21:55.460
I-I will wait for souvenir's at home... Hm?

21:55.750 --> 21:57.420
Er, Haira, where's your umbrella?

21:57.710 --> 22:00.420
Oh no, maybe it's in the worship hall?

22:00.420 --> 22:02.290
M-maybe it's in my room.

22:04.710 --> 22:06.130
Hey, Koito-chan.

22:07.130 --> 22:11.130
No matter what happens, we'll be gone before they are.

22:11.540 --> 22:17.580
Then, don't you sometimes feel like it would be better not
to be friends with them, so we don't make them upset?

22:23.710 --> 22:24.540
I do.

22:26.540 --> 22:29.130
But, I think that must be wrong.

22:31.920 --> 22:32.750
Yeah.

22:33.460 --> 22:35.960
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

22:33.710 --> 22:36.920
Have fun! Come back and see us sometime!

22:41.420 --> 22:45.920
<b>SMALL GIFT</b>

22:42.130 --> 22:43.290
"A small gift"...?

22:43.460 --> 22:45.670
For you, Elda, from Isuzu-chan.

22:45.960 --> 22:47.790
She doesn't have to thank me...

22:48.130 --> 22:50.130
She's very put together, that Isuzu...

22:51.170 --> 22:52.210
What's this?

22:52.210 --> 22:55.000
Uh... that one's a Super Rare.

22:55.000 --> 22:55.790
What?
